          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எரிச்சல் — ericcal — \"irritation; a burning feeling\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சத்தம் கேட்டு எனக்கு எரிச்சல் வந்தது. cattam kēṭṭu eṉakku ericcal vantatu. The noise irritated me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feeling comes to the person in the dative: எனக்கு எரிச்சல் (ericcal) வந்தது, literally irritation came to me. Of the body too: கண் எரிச்சல் (ericcal), stinging eyes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "எரிச்சல் (ericcal) is native Dravidian, a noun from எரி eri \"to burn\" (DEDR 811). The same entry gives the verb the sense of smarting pain and painful feeling."
            }
          ]
        },
