          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சீறு — cīṟu — \"to flare up; to hiss\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "நான் கேள்வி கேட்டேன், அவர் சீறினார். nāṉ kēḷvi kēṭṭēṉ, avar cīṟiṉār. I asked a question and he flared up."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): சீறினேன், cīṟiṉēṉ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its first sense is the hiss of a snake or the snort of a horse; of a person, a sudden angry outburst."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சீறு (cīṟu) is native Dravidian (DEDR 2639): the entry joins the hiss of a snake, the snort of a horse and a burst of rage."
            }
          ]
        },
